// check: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// CROWN crucible — the higher-order leak through a NAMED fn argument, not a
// lambda: run's param row var must ride the published scheme AND run's own
// row, so performer's closed [E] flows through the instance into bad's row.
// Born as the c01 discriminator of the 2026-08-05 dig (it proved the leak was
// not a lambda artifact); graduated when the completion prune's signature
// keep-set closed the class (Hβ.infer.hof-param-row-never-reaches-enclosing).
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn run(f) = f()
fn performer() = op()
fn bad() with !E = run(performer)
fn main() = bad()
